      "canonical_paper_id": "openalex:W2940914777",
      "title": "Robust Legged Robot State Estimation Using Factor Graph Optimization",
      "takeaway": "This work addresses legged robot state estimation when foot contact classifications fail, as on slippery or uneven terrain, and when visual odometry suffers from textureless, reflective, or occluded scenes. The authors present a factor graph optimization method that tightly fuses and smooths inertial navigation, leg odometry, and visual odometry, reducing reliance on contact classification and position drift during dynamic motions such as trotting. The approach was demonstrated on the ANYmal quadruped navigating a realistic outdoor industrial environment, including trotting, walking, crossing obstacles, and ascending a staircase, decreasing relative position error by up to 55% and absolute position error by 76% compared to kinematic-inertial odometry. While reading, inspect how the factor graph is structured and how the three odometry sources are weighted and smoothed.",
